# Line endings, pinned the same way the source repo pins them.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true, set system-wide) rewrites
# every checked-out file to CRLF, and the staging copy then reports permanent
# `drift` and `line-endings` against its source -- one warning per locale file,
# forever, on a tree that is otherwise byte-correct.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The 27 locale files and the English example are read and edited by translators
# on every platform, and a diff that is entirely line endings hides the one word
# a correction actually changed.
*.json text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must not touch them at all.
*.png binary
